1
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:11,120
Turn on the lights and
take a look from a distance.

2
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:42,800
We'll manage somehow, I'm sure.

3
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:47,160
Fahahahahahahaha!

4
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:59,900
Anyone without work, come to me.

5
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:04,480
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

6
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:18,240
Look, even the burning Akane-mu will
somehow sort itself out eventually.

7
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:27,460
You understand, right? Got it, got it. Once
you've got it, gather round and follow me.

8
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:43,620
Bonus Battle, Round 7!

9
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:01,900
Now, the 35th

10
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:06,240
we will now open the strategy meeting
for the Ryo-Tsukan-Kichi Bonus Battle.

11
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:10,040
This year's strategy will
be the Gacchari Strategy.

12
00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:11,780
Gacchari Strategy?

13
00:02:13,620 --> 00:02:20,760
That's the one, right? Where you handcuff the mass-produced
guy the day before and go to the bank together. Yes, that one.

14
00:02:21,210 --> 00:02:22,980
It's the strategy we carried out last year.

15
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:30,240
Aaaah! We were so close to succeeding...

16
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:38,600
We accidentally unlocked the handcuffs and he got away, didn't he?
Other than that one mistake, the plan was perfect.

17
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:44,000
So, this year's strategy is

18
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:49,180
the Hyper Strike-First,
Surefire Handcuff Strategy!

19
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:50,220
Hyper!

20
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:54,600
building on last year's
strike-first handcuff strategy,

21
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:58,940
we'll handcuff Ryo-san and
keep watch on him for a week.

22
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:02,020
Let's do it.

23
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:03,100
No objections.

24
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:04,820
I agree too.

25
00:03:04,820 --> 00:03:07,440
Much better than using some weird machine.

26
00:03:10,660 --> 00:03:12,980
Then, we're carrying out the operation now.

27
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:15,780
This year, we're the ones who will win!

28
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:16,400
Yeah!

29
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:22,940
It's no good! Ryo-san took the day
off yesterday and went out somewhere!

30
00:03:23,060 --> 00:03:24,720
What?

31
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:41,180
The shopping district guys must be
kicking themselves right about now.

32
00:03:41,780 --> 00:03:46,020
With this, we can withdraw our
bonus anywhere in the country.

33
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:49,720
I can't keep putting up with
those guys every single year.

34
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:54,660
Before we knew it,
he'd already submitted a leave request.

35
00:03:54,660 --> 00:03:57,080
He borrowed money from me
the day before yesterday,

36
00:03:58,320 --> 00:03:59,460
We've been played.

37
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:02,380
Ryo-san isn't stupid either.

38
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:06,400
anticipating that we'd come after him
again this year with the Gacchari strategy,

39
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:14,440
he had already made his move. Damn it, Ryo-san's instincts
are always sharp when it comes to this kind of thing.

40
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:30,380
What do we do? At this rate, we'll lose this
year's bonus before we've even done anything, Mom.

41
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:33,660
Takahashi, Takahashi.

42
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:37,080
Thanks to the cooperation of our viewers,

43
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:39,580
a mother and child who had been separated

44
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:41,980
have finally been able to reunite.

45
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:43,620
Thank you so much.

46
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:47,820
We're bringing you this live broadcast.

47
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:49,240
TV Public Investigation

48
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:51,060
We're currently looking for clients.

49
00:04:51,060 --> 00:04:53,140
For requests,
contact us right now at this number.

50
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:54,540
This is it!

51
00:04:55,960 --> 00:04:57,940
What's wrong, Plamoya-san?

52
00:04:58,600 --> 00:05:01,220
From now on,
we're changing this year's strategy.

53
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:03,920
Code-named:

54
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:07,900
It's the
"Nationwide Tearjerker Grand Reunion" operation!

55
00:05:07,900 --> 00:05:12,440
The "Nationwide Tearjerker
Grand Reunion" operation

56
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:16,380
We're not letting him get away!

57
00:05:16,380 --> 00:05:17,680
Ryo-san

58
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:24,760
So, what do we do now?

59
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:30,100
I've got the money I borrowed from Nakagawa,
so I won't go hungry for a while.

60
00:05:31,860 --> 00:05:33,340
Hey, isn't that him?

61
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:37,340
No doubt about it. We should contact him.

62
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:40,860
What, is something stuck to my face?

63
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:41,760
Yeah.

64
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:42,660
Whoa!

65
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:49,220
What is this?

66
00:05:49,220 --> 00:05:49,560
Yeah.

67
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:52,140
Whoaaa, what is it?

68
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:55,620
Wh-why is my face on TV?

69
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:58,140
His name is Kankichi Ryotsu.

70
00:05:58,140 --> 00:06:01,060
Apparently he saved the life of our client,
Mr. Ozaki.

71
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:02,220
Gah!

72
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:05,100
We really want to meet
him in person and thank him.

73
00:06:05,100 --> 00:06:05,800
Please.

74
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:10,200
Everyone across the country,
please help us find Ryo-san.

75
00:06:10,820 --> 00:06:11,180
Please!

76
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:14,700
Those guys are putting on such a phony act.

77
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:18,060
Hello, I was just watching TV.

78
00:06:18,060 --> 00:06:20,580
A man named Kankichi
Ryotsu is here right now...

79
00:06:21,140 --> 00:06:22,400
Don't report him!

80
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:24,560
I was watching the show just now.

81
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:25,700
A man named Ryotsu...

82
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:26,080
Stop it!

83
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:29,140
Hello, I saw the TV.

84
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:31,540
A man named Kankichi Ryotsu...

85
00:06:31,540 --> 00:06:33,340
Yes, he's here.

86
00:06:33,340 --> 00:06:33,880
Hello?

87
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:36,960
Uh-oh.

88
00:06:36,960 --> 00:06:39,160
If he finds out I'm here, I'm busted.

89
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:42,120
Hey, wait up!

90
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,300
Give me a ride!

91
00:06:43,300 --> 00:07:13,280
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee?

92
00:07:15,220 --> 00:07:16,080
Ryo-san!

93
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:19,980
His name is Kankichi Ryotsu-san.

94
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:22,360
He saved Mr. Ozaki's life.

95
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:25,360
We ask for the cooperation of our viewers.

96
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:29,080
Th-the soba's fine.

97
00:07:30,140 --> 00:07:30,880
Later.

98
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:33,360
Everyone across the country, please.

99
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:36,320
Please, please, Ryo-san

100
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:38,540
help us find Ryo-san.

101
00:07:39,020 --> 00:07:40,040
Ryo-san!

102
00:07:41,540 --> 00:07:42,460
Aaaaaah!

103
00:07:42,940 --> 00:07:44,160
Aaaaaah!

104
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:48,280
Damn it, we'll be too noticed in town.

105
00:07:48,280 --> 00:07:50,700
We have to go somewhere with fewer people.

106
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:05,660
Next, the tips will keep pouring in.

107
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:08,200
We might find him surprisingly soon.

108
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:10,500
No, we're dealing with Ryo-san.

109
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:19,340
Make full use of newspapers and the internet too!
Use everything you can. This year, we're the ones who win!

110
00:08:42,140 --> 00:08:45,880
Trying to avoid people's eyes,
I've ended up in some crazy place.

111
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:49,180
That's...

112
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:52,540
a police box?

113
00:08:55,420 --> 00:08:56,960
Is there nobody here?

114
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:03,640
There's no sign anyone's been here in ages.

115
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:06,500
Ahhhhhh!

116
00:09:06,500 --> 00:09:07,560
Ahhhhhh!

117
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:12,220
That police officer...

118
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:14,460
It's just...

119
00:09:16,380 --> 00:09:18,380
a real police officer.

120
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:19,440
Useless...

121
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:25,920
Hooray! A police officer has finally come to our village,
bless him!

122
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:28,320
What? What's going on?

123
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:33,120
Ever since the previous Nakaoo-san passed
away ten years ago at the age of 95,

124
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:36,380
this village has had no
police officers at all.

125
00:09:36,380 --> 00:09:38,620
So you've finally come.

126
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:42,180
No, no,
I'm not actually stationed here or anything.

127
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:43,060
Finally, hey -

128
00:09:43,060 --> 00:09:46,960
Everyone, the police have come to see us!

129
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:51,260
Hey, wait a second!
Listen to what I'm saying!

130
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:52,700
Ah, damn it.

131
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:54,600
Hey, everyone!

132
00:09:55,120 --> 00:10:01,060
The police have finally come to our village!

133
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:07,280
I have to get out of here
somehow before they report me.

134
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:17,740
It's nothing but old men and old women.

135
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,780
We'll get the welcome
party ready right away.

136
00:10:20,780 --> 00:10:22,460
Hang on a sec, I'll be right back.

137
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:31,680
Come on, come on,
let's drink, honored guest!

138
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:35,960
Gimme!

139
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:36,900
Come here.

140
00:10:40,420 --> 00:10:43,600
Even though my face has
been all over TV like that.

141
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,420
Don't any of these guys know me?

142
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:49,740
Now that I think about it,
this room doesn't even have a TV.

143
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:53,820
Hey, you guys don't watch much TV?

144
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:56,860
Sure we do, we watch it properly.

145
00:10:56,860 --> 00:11:00,680
Yep, that's right,
we all watch the Red and White once a year.

146
00:11:00,680 --> 00:11:04,120
Wait, only once a year?

147
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:06,220
Watching that much is plenty.

148
00:11:07,260 --> 00:11:10,000
By the way,
how many TVs are there in the village?

149
00:11:10,260 --> 00:11:13,200
There's one fine one at the community hall,
you know.

150
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:15,340
And it's color, color!

151
00:11:15,340 --> 00:11:16,600
Amazing, right?

152
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:19,000
I see.

153
00:11:21,420 --> 00:11:26,080
Then hiding out here until the
bonus comes in isn't such a bad idea.

154
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:28,260
Alright.

155
00:11:29,300 --> 00:11:30,920
Well then, let's drink!

156
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:35,080
Delicious.

157
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:39,940
And I'll have some of the food too.

158
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:49,240
Whoa, this is sweet! I'll bring more tomorrow too.
As long as you're in this village, don't you worry about meals.

159
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:56,940
Officer, you really came! In exchange,
please stay here with us forever, Officer.

160
00:11:56,940 --> 00:11:58,480
Yeah, there are. There are.

161
00:11:58,480 --> 00:11:59,260
Me.

162
00:12:11,760 --> 00:12:12,980
Officer!

163
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:14,560
Have you eaten breakfast?

164
00:12:15,280 --> 00:12:18,100
Sorry about that.

165
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:23,820
Well, this looks delicious.

166
00:12:24,460 --> 00:12:26,580
We grew all of this
right here in the village.

167
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:27,980
Officer.

168
00:12:27,980 --> 00:12:29,860
Something terrible has happened.

169
00:12:29,860 --> 00:12:30,880
Please come with us.

170
00:12:30,880 --> 00:12:32,740
What kind of incident is it?

171
00:12:34,340 --> 00:12:35,600
This way, this way!

172
00:12:37,460 --> 00:12:40,160
I never expected an incident in
such a remote mountain village.

173
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:46,860
The chicken's nose-thing suddenly collapsed!

174
00:12:46,860 --> 00:12:48,180
Why are you calling me?

175
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:49,780
I'm not a vet, you know.

176
00:12:49,780 --> 00:12:52,560
The previous officer took a look at it.

177
00:12:56,620 --> 00:12:58,440
Is someone home?

178
00:12:58,440 --> 00:13:01,680
No, everyone in the house has gone out.

179
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:03,120
So, a burglar?

180
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:04,080
No way.

181
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:06,940
There's no one in this village
who would do such a thing.

182
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:10,880
Someone's definitely in there.

183
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:15,340
It's coming from the kitchen, I think.

184
00:13:26,260 --> 00:13:27,280
Don't move!

185
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:31,980
You're the cow Hanataro!

186
00:13:31,980 --> 00:13:32,340
What?

187
00:13:38,260 --> 00:13:39,380
What was that just now?

188
00:13:40,020 --> 00:13:42,060
It's Hanataro,
the one we kept at home long ago.

189
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:44,520
One day he suddenly ran off from home

190
00:13:44,520 --> 00:13:47,820
and teamed up with his buddies to become
a marauder terrorizing the village.

191
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:49,480
What a cow.

192
00:13:51,620 --> 00:13:53,720
You were supposed to be knocked out!

193
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:56,100
Damn it.

194
00:13:57,320 --> 00:13:58,260
Did he get away?

195
00:14:00,700 --> 00:14:01,500
Hanataro

196
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:03,640
He was in on it too.

197
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:08,420
Oh no, even Hanataro has
gone down the wrong path!

198
00:14:08,940 --> 00:14:11,620
Officer, do something about this!

199
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:15,220
I'm not the animal control office!
Sort it out yourselves!

200
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,980
I was sure I closed the door.

201
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:25,980
We've been hit. Did those guys do this?

202
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:30,380
Even the games and model
kits I brought to kill time!

203
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:35,600
That damn cow! I'll never forgive him!

204
00:14:44,640 --> 00:14:45,840
Found you!

205
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:46,960
It's that cow too!

206
00:14:52,140 --> 00:14:53,160
Don't you dare lay a hand on that!

207
00:14:59,240 --> 00:14:59,960
Wait!

208
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:03,640
Don't think you can anger
me and get away with it!

209
00:15:17,260 --> 00:15:19,020
Fool, you fell for it.

210
00:15:19,020 --> 00:15:21,640
In the end, we can never beat you humans.

211
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:26,320
Thank you, thank you.

212
00:15:30,980 --> 00:15:34,140
To catch Hanataro so easily like this!

213
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:36,140
As expected of a police officer, dang.

214
00:15:36,140 --> 00:15:39,200
Please stay in the
village even one day longer.

215
00:15:39,940 --> 00:15:45,140
If you lot defy me any further, it's steak,
tonkatsu, and roast chicken for you.

216
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:50,540
What on earth is going on?

217
00:15:51,060 --> 00:15:53,280
And the day after tomorrow is bonus day.

218
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:56,040
We haven't gotten any
information about Ryo-san at all.

219
00:15:56,700 --> 00:15:58,520
Didn't he flee overseas?

220
00:15:59,100 --> 00:16:02,340
If he went to an airport or a port,
he'd surely be noticed.

221
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:03,780
He must be in disguise.

222
00:16:03,780 --> 00:16:08,000
Even in disguise, that unibrow
of his can't stay hidden for long.

223
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:10,760
The river does have
distinctive features, so.

224
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:13,620
Then where is Ryo-san right now?!

225
00:16:13,900 --> 00:16:16,880
Isn't he hiding out in
some countryside somewhere?

226
00:16:16,980 --> 00:16:19,000
Somewhere without TV reception,
or something like that.

227
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:20,520
That's it!

228
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:25,520
The last sighting was here.

229
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:27,960
Should we set a net here
and hope for the best?

230
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:33,940
Looks like the autumn
typhoon knocked it out.

231
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:36,820
You hardly watch TV anyway, right?

232
00:16:36,820 --> 00:16:40,620
But we'd be in trouble if it
isn't fixed by New Year's Eve.

233
00:16:40,920 --> 00:16:43,240
Because the whole village watches the Red and White together,
you see.

234
00:16:44,060 --> 00:16:45,000
Well.

235
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:50,600
How's that? Is it showing?

236
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:52,820
Whoa! Crystal clear!

237
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:55,660
Regarding that statement just now,
Mr. Akimoto is completely...

238
00:16:55,660 --> 00:16:57,880
It's been ages since we've watched TV.

239
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:00,280
Here's the next news.

240
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:04,120
Today, civil servants' bonuses
were paid out all at once.

241
00:17:04,827 --> 00:17:08,600
It feels like I'm forgetting
something important...

242
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,620
Today's my bonus day too!

243
00:17:11,940 --> 00:17:14,240
Damn it! I can't be wasting time like this!

244
00:17:17,440 --> 00:17:18,780
Oh no, this is bad!

245
00:17:21,740 --> 00:17:24,960
The officer! The officer's leaving!

246
00:17:29,700 --> 00:17:31,620
Damn! So he won't be back for a while!

247
00:17:31,620 --> 00:17:34,300
Should we borrow a tractor
from the villagers or something?

248
00:17:34,300 --> 00:17:35,680
Officer.

249
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:38,020
Perfect timing, right?

250
00:17:44,540 --> 00:17:47,580
Where are you off to, Officer?

251
00:17:48,220 --> 00:17:49,240
Where?

252
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:51,720
I just suddenly remembered something.

253
00:17:53,220 --> 00:17:56,660
You said you'd stay here for good,
didn't you?

254
00:17:57,400 --> 00:17:59,940
No, no,
I'm just going out for a little while.

255
00:18:02,480 --> 00:18:03,720
Is that true?

256
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:21,280
You're our village officer,
aren't you, officer?

257
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:23,600
You'll stay with us forever, won't you?

258
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:27,300
If you have errands, we'll go in your place.

259
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:31,175
Well, th-the truth is, I've received
a transfer order from headquarters,

260
00:18:31,225 --> 00:18:34,080
telling me to return to Tokyo.

261
00:18:34,620 --> 00:18:36,860
Thanks for all the help you've given me.

262
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:39,380
What, you're going to abandon us?!

263
00:18:39,780 --> 00:18:41,440
You promised!

264
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:54,420
No way! At this rate, I'll be stuck
as this village's officer until I die!

265
00:18:57,060 --> 00:18:58,140
Wait there!

266
00:18:58,560 --> 00:19:02,580
Hup!

267
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:06,980
You bastard!

268
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:09,660
The officer's getting away!

269
00:19:09,820 --> 00:19:11,000
Cut him off!

270
00:19:18,140 --> 00:19:19,560
If we get this far,

271
00:19:29,300 --> 00:19:31,340
once he passes that tunnel,

272
00:19:34,020 --> 00:19:36,200
What, are you planning to block the tunnel?

273
00:19:52,420 --> 00:19:53,960
Yes, the escape worked!

274
00:19:56,420 --> 00:19:56,780
Let's go!

275
00:20:04,154 --> 00:20:07,220
the police line...

276
00:20:07,220 --> 00:20:09,320
He's gone...

277
00:20:12,640 --> 00:20:22,220
W-what was that just now...?

278
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:34,820
We got the bonus!

279
00:20:35,420 --> 00:20:37,320
Things have gotten so convenient lately,
haven't they?

280
00:20:37,320 --> 00:20:40,520
You can withdraw money at any bank now.

281
00:20:40,520 --> 00:20:43,940
Honestly,
things have become so convenient these days.

282
00:20:43,940 --> 00:20:46,100
That voice...

283
00:20:49,180 --> 00:20:51,440
Quietly hand over that bonus

284
00:20:51,440 --> 00:20:54,580
to us.

285
00:20:56,420 --> 00:20:57,660
And there I am!

286
00:20:58,060 --> 00:20:59,883
Based on eyewitness reports,

287
00:20:59,933 --> 00:21:02,640
we analyzed your movements,
and this is the result.

288
00:21:02,640 --> 00:21:03,760
Damn it!

289
00:21:04,080 --> 00:21:05,880
Give up, Ryo-san.

290
00:21:06,420 --> 00:21:08,440
Now, hand over the bonus!

291
00:21:11,180 --> 00:21:12,240
The bonus...

292
00:21:19,200 --> 00:21:20,340
The pig's got the bonus!

293
00:21:20,340 --> 00:21:23,760
Hey! That's my bonus! Give it back!

294
00:21:27,820 --> 00:21:28,900
Wait up!

295
00:21:29,460 --> 00:21:30,960
We'll chase it too!

296
00:21:35,800 --> 00:21:38,640
We won't let it escape!

297
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:42,320
Why is a pig running
off with Ryo-san's bonus!

298
00:21:42,620 --> 00:21:45,560
That's Ryo-san's, all right!
He must have done something here too!

299
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:48,760
Get back here!

300
00:21:49,020 --> 00:21:49,900
Get back here!

301
00:22:00,300 --> 00:22:03,200
We can't just stand here forever!

302
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:06,060
We'll just have to wait for
someone else to come along!

303
00:22:06,980 --> 00:22:07,960
But...

304
00:22:09,680 --> 00:22:11,260
That voice?

305
00:22:11,520 --> 00:22:12,780
It's the police officer!

306
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:14,860
Officer!

307
00:22:15,240 --> 00:22:16,700
He came back!

308
00:22:24,580 --> 00:22:26,080
Wait, wait!

309
00:22:26,380 --> 00:22:29,520
Wh-what?

310
00:22:31,280 --> 00:22:32,500
Wait!

311
00:22:51,900 --> 00:22:53,460
The trash can -

312
00:22:53,460 --> 00:22:56,400
my house -

313
00:22:56,780 --> 00:22:59,480
our field -

314
00:22:59,480 --> 00:23:01,400
what a mess this is!

315
00:23:02,880 --> 00:23:04,200
the hot spring -

316
00:23:10,440 --> 00:23:32,660
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

317
00:23:32,660 --> 00:23:34,640
The cow ate our bonus!

318
00:23:38,920 --> 00:23:40,420
The back is a total wreck!

319
00:23:40,420 --> 00:23:44,280
I knew that cop shouldn't have come back.

320
00:23:44,780 --> 00:23:45,480
Yeah, that's right.

321
00:23:45,480 --> 00:23:48,240
Damn! We didn't win again this year!

322
00:23:48,240 --> 00:23:50,260
Stop jumping around, will you!

323
00:23:50,940 --> 00:23:52,040
The bonus -

324
00:23:52,040 --> 00:23:54,300
my bonus -

325
00:23:55,380 --> 00:23:58,060
my bonus!

326
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:53,500
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten.

327
00:24:54,600 --> 00:24:57,580
Politicians with their big-shot faces,

328
00:24:57,580 --> 00:25:00,940
and aunties with blue eyeshadow, too.

329
00:25:00,940 --> 00:25:06,520
Go on, turn that corner over there.

330
00:25:07,700 --> 00:25:11,680
You'll get to meet everyone, everyone!

331
00:25:11,680 --> 00:25:12,700
Don't go!

332
00:25:12,700 --> 00:25:16,360
Over there, there are turtles,

333
00:25:17,560 --> 00:25:19,700
well, surely there are turtles.

334
00:25:21,160 --> 00:25:24,860
Everyone, come on over to our town!

335
00:25:26,040 --> 00:25:26,440
Thank you.

336
00:25:30,860 --> 00:25:31,660
What?

337
00:25:31,780 --> 00:25:35,140
Did the land Grandpa Minoxi left
behind sell for 1 billion yen?

338
00:25:35,340 --> 00:25:37,360
Talk about a windfall out of nowhere!

339
00:25:37,360 --> 00:25:38,640
Like a rice cake falling from the shelf!

340
00:25:38,640 --> 00:25:39,640
Easy money!

341
00:25:39,640 --> 00:25:43,320
If that's how it is,
I'm gonna blow this billion yen big time!

342
00:25:43,800 --> 00:25:47,180
Next time,
"From a Gourd, a Billion Yen." See you then!

343
00:25:52,740 --> 00:25:53,140
Thank you.

